><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">62.7&#x00025;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">73.5&#x00025;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">73.8&#x00025;</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td></tr><tr><td colspan="4" align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><italic>Scenario 9: Decreased HPV type distribution of 16/18 in cervical cancer</italic></td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.356&#x00025;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">749</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">397</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x02003;&#x00025; Reduction</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">66.7&#x00025;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">71.6&#x00025;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">71.7&#x00025;</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="t4-fn1"><label>a</label><p>Base case assumes 95&#x00025; efficacy against 16 and 18 infection, 50&#x00025; efficacy against HPV 31, 90&#x00025; efficacy against HPV 45. No waning is assumed. Results are provided for 100&#x00025; vaccine coverage.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>